The MIT licence above covers the LosslessCam application sources
(LosslessCam/, LosslessBridge/, scripts/, .github/). The binary built by the
GitHub Actions workflow additionally contains the third-party components
listed below, each under its own licence.


Third-party components
----------------------

FFmpeg (libavcodec, libavformat, libavutil)
    https://ffmpeg.org — Copyright (c) 2000-2026 the FFmpeg developers
    Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later
    (LGPL-2.1-or-later). scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh builds FFmpeg from the pinned
    upstream tag with --disable-gpl --disable-nonfree, so no GPL or non-free
    component is included; the resulting libraries are LGPL. The exact
    configure line is recorded in ThirdParty/ffmpeg/BUILD_INFO.txt of every
    build. Per LGPL section 6, the FFmpeg source corresponding to the binaries
    is the tagged upstream release named in scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh, and the
    application links FFmpeg as static libraries whose object files can be
    relinked by rebuilding from this repository. The FFmpeg licence text is at
    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html.

    The app displays the FFmpeg version, licence and configure line under
    Settings -> About.

xxHash (ThirdParty/xxhash/xxhash.h)
    https://github.com/Cyan4973/xxHash — Copyright (c) 2012-2023 Yann Collet
